/target
/Cargo.lock
artifacts/

# Generated libFuzzer corpus entries (issue #419). `cargo fuzz run` writes a new file per
# interesting input straight into this directory, so a local fuzzing session leaves the
# tree full of stageable binary blobs and the runner has to clean up by hand before
# committing.
#
# The CURATED seeds are kept, and the rule is exact rather than approximate: every corpus
# entry this repository tracks is named `seed_*` (one per `seed_*` file; the tests in the crate assert the floors, which is the
# version that cannot drift), and libFuzzer
# names what it generates after the hash of the contents, so the two populations cannot
# collide. Adding a new seed therefore needs no `git add -f`.
corpus/**
!corpus/**/
!corpus/**/seed_*
